\section*{Symbolic intensity equations}

\subsection*{T2g}

Cubic benchmark VV: (500); CUBIC\_VV\par

\[\fitmath{I(\theta)=- \frac{d \cos{\left(4 \theta \right)} \overline{d}}{2} + \frac{d \overline{d}}{2}}\]

\begingroup\small\noindent\textbf{Symbols and units}\par\smallskip

\noindent$\theta;\ \theta_i,\theta_s$: Theta is the common linear-polarization scan angle for VV/VH. In the general direct-state product, theta\_i and theta\_s instead denote the incident and detection mixing angles. \textit{Unit / convention:} rad in formulas; degree in input and angle CSV columns\par\smallskip

\noindent$d$: Independent complex tensor coefficients in the selected symmetry form. Only symbols actually used in this equation are active. For Si T2g the three partner tensors share d. \textit{Unit / convention:} relative tensor-coefficient units\par\smallskip

\noindent$I,I_j;\ I_0,I_c,I_s,I_{4c},I_{4s};\ I_{min},I_{max}$: Relative intensity, its real harmonic coefficients and extrema. The final j sum adds intensities of unresolved orthogonal phonon partners. Coherent tensor terms within one partner are added before squaring. \textit{Unit / convention:} squared relative tensor-coefficient units, plotted as a.u.\par\smallskip

\noindent${}^*,\overline{\phantom a};\ {}^\dagger$: Complex conjugation and conjugate transpose. The detection state must be conjugated before contraction. \textit{Unit / convention:} operation; conjugation preserves units\par\smallskip

\noindent\textit{Derivation / source:} Tensor/intensity principle: Pimenta Eqs. (2)-(4); conjugate detector and Si partner sum: Paukatong Eqs. (9),(11). Intermediate products, harmonics and extrema are program algebra; QWP source convention follows Kumar where selected.\par

\noindent \href{https://doi.org/10.1039/D1CP03626B}{Pimenta et al. (2021)}; Section 1.1, Eqs. (1)-(4); Section 1.2; linear-polarization discussion in Section 2\par

\noindent \href{https://doi.org/10.1002/jrs.70113}{Paukatong et al. (2026)}; Section 2.1, Eqs. (1)-(6); Section 2.2, Eqs. (9) and (11)\par

\noindent \href{https://faizal-07-script.github.io/rotation-raman-tensor-calculation/downloads/Dr_Kumar_Original.ipynb}{Kumar-san, supplied original notebook (2026-10-15)}; Original Cells 2-11 and the separately labeled appendix\par

\noindent Program algebra, Cells 6, 11 and 12; Algebra of the displayed tensors and Jones states\par

\noindent \href{https://www.nist.gov/pml/special-publication-811/nist-guide-si-chapter-7-rules-and-style-conventions-expressing-values}{NIST, Guide to the SI, Section 7.10}; Section 7.10: dimension-one quantities and the radian\par

\endgroup\end{document}

